# 18. SECURITY AND CLIENT DATA ISOLATION

Security is mandatory.

Implement Supabase Row Level Security (RLS) on all client-owned data.

A client may only access records associated with their authenticated user identity.

Enforce authorization on the backend as well as the database.

Required protections:

- Secure authentication.
- Verified client identity.
- Role-based access control.
- Client ownership verification.
- RLS policies.
- Server-side validation.
- Input sanitization.
- Rate limiting.
- CSRF protection where applicable.
- Secure HTTP headers.
- Session expiration.
- Audit logging.
- Secure file access.
- Payment webhook verification.
- Idempotency for payment and credit operations.

Never rely on frontend route protection as the only security control.

Never trust client-submitted:
- Prices
- Discounts
- Credit balances
- Payment statuses
- Order totals
- Subscription statuses
- Project ownership
- Administrative roles

All sensitive calculations and state changes must be performed and verified server-side.

